        <section id="responsive-reflow">
          <span class="step-badge">STAGE 07</span>
          <h2>Responsive Reflow via Container Queries</h2>
          <p>
            Traditional websites rely on global viewport media queries (e.g., <code>@media (max-width: 768px)</code>). If a layout is embedded in a sidebar, a modal, or an iframe, viewport media queries fail because they measure the whole screen instead of the component's actual space.
          </p>
          <p>
            Kōshi uses <strong>native CSS Container Queries</strong>. Every <code>.kos-composition</code> creates its own containment context:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Above <code>48rem</code> container width: all 12 fractional tracks, multi-row spans, and offsets operate in full editorial richness.</li>
            <li>Below <code>48rem</code> container width: Kōshi automatically reflows multi-column grids into a clean, comfortable single-column reading stack.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            You can customize collapse thresholds per section using the <code>kos-collapse</code> attribute:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><code>kos-collapse="sm"</code>: Collapses at <code>32rem</code> (mobile phones only).</li>
            <li><code>kos-collapse="md"</code>: Default collapse at <code>48rem</code> (tablets & phones).</li>
            <li><code>kos-collapse="lg"</code>: Collapses early at <code>64rem</code> (compact laptops).</li>
            <li><code>kos-collapse="none"</code>: Retains strict 12-column layout at all widths.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

